From: ilex
Subject: [PATCH] homed: apply the user limit to enumerated users

local_users contains every entry from /etc/shadow, including system users.
On Fedora's desktop image its size exceeds MAX_LOCAL_USERS before homed is
enumerated. Bound the human-user table, as the other generators do.

Source: Fedora accountsservice-26.27.3-2.fc45.src.rpm, src/daemon.c
Remove this backport once the Fedora package includes the fix.

--- a/src/daemon.c
+++ b/src/daemon.c
@@ -709,7 +709,7 @@ entry_generator_homed (Daemon         *daemon,
 
         /* Every ieration */
         s = *state;
-        if (g_hash_table_size (local_users) < MAX_LOCAL_USERS) {
+        if (g_hash_table_size (users) < MAX_LOCAL_USERS) {
                 g_autofree char *status = NULL;
 
                 homed_clear_pwent (&s->pwent);
